772323200,2.4],[1775001600,5.6],[1777593600,8.0],[1780272000,10.3],[1782864000,12.0],[1785542400,10.5],[1788220800,6.0]]},{"id":"nondurables","name":"Consumer non-durables","units":"Per cent","pts":[[1680307200,0.6],[1682899200,8.4],[1685577600,6.9],[1688169600,5.0],[1690848000,8.7],[1693526400,6.4],[1696118400,3.3],[1698796800,2.9],[1701388800,15.5],[1704067200,10.6],[1706745600,9.6],[1709251200,14.5],[1711929600,5.1],[1714521600,2.0],[1717200000,5.1],[1719792000,3.4],[1722470400,2.9],[1725148800,4.1],[1727740800,8.8],[1730419200,4.0],[1733011200,-0.5],[1735689600,4.7],[1738368000,-0.5],[1740787200,4.8],[1743465600,3.3],[1746057600,3.3],[1748736000,-2.0],[1751328000,5.8],[1754006400,0.1],[1756684800,-0.5],[1759276800,-9.4],[1761955200,3.9],[1764547200,5.9],[1767225600,-1.2],[1769904000,1.6],[1772323200,-0.6],[1775001600,0.2],[1777593600,-0.4],[1780272000,5.6],[1782864000,-0.8],[1785542400,-1.1],[1788220800,1.4]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the use-based IIP measure?","answer":"The Index of Industrial Production (IIP), compiled by MoSPI's National Statistics Office, tracks the volume of output of a fixed basket of industrial products. The use-based classification regroups the same items by how the goods are used: primary goods (basic inputs such as minerals, electricity-generation fuels, raw materials), capital goods (machinery and equipment used to produce other goods), intermediate goods (inputs used in further processing), infrastructure/construction goods (cement, steel products, paints, cables and similar), consumer durables and consumer non-durables.^Capital goods output is a read on investment demand, infrastructure/construction goods on building and public capex, and the two consumer groups on household demand, so the split is more informative for nowcasting than the headline."},{"question":"How should I read the index and the growth rate?","answer":"Index levels are relative to the base year average (=100), so 130 means 30 per cent above the base-year average. Levels are strongly seasonal (March is typically the peak, and the festive months move with Diwali timing), so use year-on-year growth, which compares the same month, for momentum. The growth rate here is the one published by MoSPI; the year-ago index for the early months of the new series is not published, so the published growth is shown instead of recomputing it.^Base effects matter: the quick estimate for a month is revised in the next two releases, so compare latest growth with caution."},{"question":"Definitions, revisions and caveats","answer":"MoSPI rebased the IIP to 2022-23=100 with the new series (starting April 2023). Index levels of the new and old (2011-12=100) series cannot be compared or chained directly; the old series ends in March 2026 and is shown in its own record. Each month is a quick estimate (QE) at first release and gets a final revision in the following month's release.^In the 2022-23 series the use-based weights (per cent of the index) are primary 31.1, capital 8.1, intermediate 22.4, infrastructure/construction 10.9, consumer durables 11.3 and consumer non-durables 16.1 (as printed in MoSPI's press release). Data are fetched from MoSPI's public eSankhyiki API."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Base 2022-23=100 only; not comparable in level with the 2011-12=100 record. The 2011-12 series is shown separately.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:22:47+00:00"}